    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="37c4ec0e-41e8-5f91-8a01-b4c6e5fa4ef7" activityNameId="335d342d-24d7-555a-9e83-e3c944a8a0ae" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, sewer system, reinforced concrete pipe, DN 600, profile 2</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, sewer system, reinforced concrete pipe, DN 600, profile 2
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: ae477a2b-433b-42f6-b272-a964df329687
This process models deconstruction and end-of-life treatment for 1 meter of installed sewer infrastructure with reinforced concrete pipe. DN 600, profile 2 according to SIA 190. Trench depth: 3 meters. This process includes the deconstruction phase (C1), transport phase (C2), treatment/ recycling phase (C3), and final disposal phase (C4) for 1 meter of sewer system with reinforced concrete pipe, DN 600, profile 2. The operation of similar types of building machines across different processes is aggregated to one process.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: DN 600, profile 2 according to SIA 190.Trench depth 3 meters. Reinforced concrete pipe, 600 mm, outer diameter 780 mm, wall thickness 90 mm, 540 kg/m, 2770 kg/m³
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_ae477a2b-433b-42f6-b272-a964df329687.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
